Parameter:
  (<Article number>)

Description:
  Removes praise that you previously gave to an article in the current
  conference.

  If no article number is given, praise is removed from the article you
  last read. If you give an article number, your praise is removed from
  that article.

  Removing praise lowers the article's praise count. The article also
  disappears from the list of articles you have praised.

Observe:
  You can only remove your own praise. Praise from other users is not
  affected.

  If you have not praised the selected article, nothing is changed.

  Unpraise is only available in local conferences, not in your Mailbox,
  Usenet conferences, or FTN conferences.

Background:
  Unpraise belongs to the praise feature, which was added in October
  2025. The command removes your entry from the conference's !(hiss)
  data.
